## Report & block

`modules/moderation/`, which both app stores require for user-generated
content. The Flutter moarch's ModerationService calls it:
`POST /moderation/reports` `{type, targetId, reason, details}`,
`POST /moderation/blocks` `{userId}`, `DELETE /moderation/blocks/{userId}`,
`GET /moderation/blocks`. All need a signed-in user.

Reports land in `moderation_reports` with status `open`; review them from
your admin tool or the database, promptly (the stores expect it). A module
that shows what users publish must filter with `blocked_user_ids` and
`is_blocked_between` from `modules/moderation/public.py`: the app only hides
what it is sent.
